    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106023" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῡρός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cheese,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δ᾽ αἴγειον κνῆ τυρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.639
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἐπιδευὴς τυροῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.88
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐξ Ἀχαΐης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. Σικελικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					896
				</span></i>
			, etc.; for Sicilian cheese, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				63.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				236
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				76
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				110.25
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ χλωρὸς τ.</span> the fresh
			<i>cheese,</i> hence <i>the cheese-market,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				23.6
			</span></i>.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βούτυρον.</span></div>
